  "question": {
    "text": "The equilibrium constant of the following isomerisation reaction at <math> <mrow> <mtext>400</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>K</mtext></mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mtext>298</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>K</mtext></mrow> </math> are <math> <mrow> <mtext>2</mtext><mtext>.07</mtext></mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mtext>3</mtext><mtext>.42</mtext></mrow> </math> respectively.<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/pxykewhronxzhthpfahykuzychjoixgbfkfvlmkaqkazmcipge.jpeg\" style=\"height: 45px; width: 250px;\" /><br />\rWhich of the following is/are correct?<br />\rI. The reaction is exothermic<br />\rII. The reaction is endothermic<br />\rIII. At <math> <mrow> <mtext>400</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>K</mtext></mrow> </math> <math> <mrow> <mtext>50%</mtext></mrow> </math> of cis-butene and <math> <mrow> <mtext>50%</mtext></mrow> </math> of trans-butene are present of equilibrium<br />\rIV. Both at <math> <mrow> <mtext>298</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>K</mtext></mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mn>400</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>K</mtext></mrow> </math>, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
